<style>
/* Motor styling */
.rm-motor-wrap {
  max-width: 1300px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 0 14px 22px;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  color: #1b1b1b;
}

.rm-motor-card {
  border: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,.12);
  border-radius: 14px;
  overflow: hidden;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 26px rgba(0,0,0,.08);
  margin: 14px 0;
  background: #fff;
}

.rm-motor-head-1b {
  padding: 14px 16px;
  background: #bc9923;
  color: #fff;
}

.rm-motor-head-1dab {
  padding: 14px 16px;
  background: #bc9923;
  color: #fff;
}

.rm-motor-head-2b {
  padding: 14px 16px;
  background: #1d3748;
  color: #fff;
}

.rm-motor-head-2dab {
  padding: 14px 16px;
  background: #1d3748;
  color: #fff;
}

.rm-motor-head-4hd {
  padding: 14px 16px;
  background: #5d3324;
  color: #fff;
}

.rm-motor-head-6 {
  padding: 14px 16px;
  background: #2c5f2d;
  color: #fff;
}

.rm-motor-head-1b h3,
.rm-motor-head-1dab h3,
.rm-motor-head-2b h3,
.rm-motor-head-2dab h3,
.rm-motor-head-4hd h3,
.rm-motor-head-6 h3 {
  margin: 0;
  margin-bottom: 5px;
  font-size: 20px;
  font-weight: 800;
  letter-spacing: .2px;
}

.rm-motor-sub {
  margin: 6px 0 0;
  font-size: 13px;
  opacity: .9;
  font-weight: 600;
}

.rm-motor-body {
  padding: 14px 16px 16px;
}

.rm-motor-body p {
  margin: 0 0 10px;
  line-height: 1.45;
}

.rm-motor-feats {
  margin: 10px 0 0;
  padding: 0;
  list-style: none;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
  gap: 8px 14px;
}

.rm-motor-feats li {
  margin: 0;
  padding-left: 22px;
  position: relative;
  line-height: 1.35;
}

.rm-motor-feats li:before {
  content: "✓";
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  top: 0;
  color: #0a7a2f;
  font-weight: 900;
}

.rm-motor-note {
  margin-top: 10px;
  padding: 10px 12px;
  border-radius: 12px;
  background: rgba(129,15,18,.08);
  border: 1px solid rgba(129,15,18,.18);
  color: #2a2a2a;
  font-size: 13px;
  line-height: 1.35;
}

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .rm-motor-feats {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}
</style>

{% if DAB %}
<!-- Main Content Section -->
<div style="display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; padding: 20px; gap: 20px; max-width: 100%;">
  <!-- Image Section -->
<div style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;</div>
<!-- Description Section -->
<div style="flex: 2; min-width: 300px; padding: 10px;">
<h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; color: #333;">{{ product.title }}</h2>
<p>
    The RetroSound Monza Radio Face brings understated European styling to the DIN Solutions lineup, designed specifically for classic vehicles with factory Single DIN openings. Inspired by the clean, driver-focused dashboards found in vintage BMW, Jaguar, Mercedes-Benz, and MGB interiors, the Monza delivers a subtle, period-correct appearance with modern audio capability.
  </p>
  <p>
    Its fully blacked-out face, low-profile push-buttons, and minimalist layout blend naturally into classic interiors without the oversized styling common in modern aftermarket radios. Two included knob styles allow owners to tailor the appearance to better match the character of their vehicle.
  </p>
  <p>
    Part of the RetroSound DIN Solutions line, the Monza pairs with RetroSound's modular radio motor system, allowing enthusiasts to select the feature set that best fits their needs. Depending on the selected motor, users can add modern functionality such as Bluetooth&reg; connectivity, USB media playback, advanced audio controls, and app compatibility while preserving the clean aesthetic of the dashboard.
  </p>

<!-- Key Features Box -->
<section class="rm-motor-card" style="margin-top: 20px;">
  <div style="padding: 14px 16px; background: #2a2a2a; color: #fff;">
    <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 800; letter-spacing: .2px;">Key Features</h3>
    <div style="margin: 6px 0 0; font-size: 13px; opacity: .9; font-weight: 600;">Clean All-Black Styling &bull; Standard Single-DIN &bull; RetroSound&reg; Modular System</div>
  </div>
  <div class="rm-motor-body">
    <ul class="rm-motor-feats">
      <li>Clean all-black styling inspired by classic European dashboards</li>
      <li>Designed for BMW, Jaguar, Mercedes-Benz, MGB, and other European classics</li>
      <li>Fits standard Single DIN radio openings</li>
      <li>Includes two interchangeable front knob styles</li>
      <li>Compatible with RetroSound modular radio motors</li>
      <li>Available feature sets range from essential playback to advanced connectivity</li>
      <li>Bluetooth&reg;, USB, HD Radio&reg;, and app support available depending on selected motor</li>
      <li>Low-profile push-buttons and minimalist factory-style appearance</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
</div>

